{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpkKP1PNhXJBCBkobb1c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It's not ESM-only. `require('@modelcontextprotocol/server')` works.\n\nI checked the published manifest for the latest version, **v2.3.1**, on the npm registry:\n\n- `\"type\": \"module\"` is set, so the package defaults to ESM, but it also ships a CommonJS build.\n- `exports[\".\"]` has both conditions:\n  - `import` → `./dist/index.mjs` (types: `index.d.mts`)\n  - `require` → `./dist/index.cjs` (types: `index.d.cts`)\n- `./stdio` follows the same pattern (`stdio.mjs` / `stdio.cjs`), so `require('@modelcontextprotocol/server/stdio')` works too.\n- `\"main\": \"./dist/index.cjs\"` is a fallback for older tools that don't read `exports`.\n- It needs Node 20 or newer (`\"engines\": {\"node\": \">=20\"}`).\n\nSome things to watch for:\n- **TypeScript:** set `moduleResolution` to `node16`, `nodenext` or `bundler` so it picks up the `exports` map and the `.d.cts` types. The legacy `node`/`node10` setting ignores `exports`, so `require` of subpaths like `/stdio` won't type-check.\n- **Dual-package hazard:** if your app loads the package through both `import` and `require`, it gets two separate copies of the module. Pick one style and use it everywhere.\n- I only checked the root and `./stdio` entries. The other subpaths (`./validators/ajv`, `./validators/cf-worker`, `./_shims`) probably follow the same pattern, but I didn't confirm it. Also, `@modelcontextprotocol/client` and the other v2 packages publish their own manifests, so check each one separately.\n\nLudion had no lessons on this, so this answer comes only from the registry data.\n\nSources:\n- [npm registry: @modelcontextprotocol/server@latest](https://registry.npmjs.org/@modelcontextprotocol/server/latest)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":506,"cache_r